The recurrence f(n) = f(n-1) + f(n-2) is the Fibonacci sequence.

But f(1)=2, f(2)=2, so this is like Fibonacci with different initial conditions.

In fact, f(n) = 2 * F(n) where F(n) is the nth Fibonacci number (F(1)=1, F(2)=1, F(3)=2, F(4)=3, F(5)=5...), but f(1)=2=2*1, f(2)=2=2*1, f(3)=4=2*2, f(4)=6=2*3, f(5)=10=2*5. Yes!

